\subsection{Finite-Sample V- vs.\ U-Energy Estimators}
Table~5 keeps all $n_c, m_c \ge 1$ cells (3/10 raw, 1/10 centered clean V FRR on E). Table~7 compares V and U estimators on shared $n_c, m_c \ge 2$ cells (18--20 in B; 19--20 in E without \texttt{rgb\_warm|zh} on \texttt{gw-gemini-3.6-flash}, giving 2/10 raw, 1/10 centered clean V FRR under matched B3v3 cutoffs). At $\delta_0=15$, the unbiased U numerator cuts clean E EER from 10.00\% to 0.00\%--1.11\% and frozen FRR from 20.00\% to 10.00\% without the 256-draw bootstrap. Unregularized $\Denergy{}$ also reaches 0.00\% EER / 10.00\% FRR cleanly, but suffers 100.00\% jitter FRR and 6.04\% $\mathrm{CF0}\rightarrow\mathrm{CF21}$ B3v3 FAR. Under $\pm 8$ jitter on E, the U numerator, signed ratio, and clipped ratio yield 8.89\%, 1.11\%, and 2.44\% EER vs.\ 13.00\%, 37.00\%, and 21.00\% frozen FRR (0.00\% FAR); ranking and fixed cutoffs diverge. Signed U-ratio $\mathrm{CF21}\rightarrow\mathrm{OR21}$ FRR drops from 21.43\% (B3v3) to 0.00\% under B6v6.

